00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.230 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  after months of distance education the  clark county school district now has a  plan for getting kids  back into the classroom thank you for  joining us tonight at 11 i'm bryan  loftis  and i'm denise valdez ccsd's plan is  actually a hybrid model so it's a  combination of at home  and in person learning oracle mana  joining us now live in the studio  tonight to explain how it will all look  for students orca  well denise and brian this 250 page plan  released tonight  by ccsd really shows how much thought is  going into this  now under the hybrid model students will  start getting back in the classroom  in january it's important to note that  this is just a proposal it'll be voted  on later this week  and teachers and parents i spoke to have  differing opinions on it  i would love to go back in the classroom  the clark county school district is now  closer to making that happen ccsd  releasing this plan to transition to the  hybrid model after months of remote  learning  students would be divided into three  groups two would do a mix of in-person  and at-home learning and the third would  do full-time distance education and now  for the first time we have return dates  on december 1st all employees would go  to work locations on january 4th  students in pre-k to second grade 6th  grade and 11th to 12th grade would begin  hybrid learning and on january 11th all  other grades would start the proposed  plan details capping classroom sizes to  50 percent  and it even provides visual aids on how  to space out desks to adhere to social  distancing guidelines  additionally no playground equipment  water fountains or field trips would be  allowed some after school activities  would be ok  including no contact or minimal contact  sports social distancing and better air  flow is recommended on school buses mask  wearing and extra sanitation would also  be required even with these measures not  everyone is convinced  i appreciate the plan but at the same  time i'm definitely concerned especially  with the way that the numbers are  getting out of control again  also a concern for many the impact of  distance learning on the mental health  and academic progress of students  ccsd noting an increased student suicide  rate and falling grades some parents say  that needs to change  i would love for the kids to go back to  school again  in a very safe environment that's safe  and healthy and hygienic for them and  the employees  but nothing really beats face-to-face  learning and being in the same room as  the person you're learning from  now it's important to note that several  charter and private schools in the  valley have been doing everything from  a hybrid model to full in classroom  learning for months  now the ccsc board of trustees will vote  on the district's plan  at their meeting this thursday night

